# MCP routing

Use the configured MCP servers by task type. Do not call every MCP on every message.

**Enabled MCPs:** `context7`, `ollama-fast`, `perplexity-coding`, `perplexity-search`

## MCP visibility (required)

At the **start** of each Agent response (before the main answer):

**MCPs used:** `none` | `context7` | `ollama-fast` | `perplexity-coding` | `perplexity-search` (comma-separated if multiple)

**Why:** One line explaining the routing choice.

- List only MCPs **actually called** this turn.
- If repo tools only: `MCPs used: none`.
- On **escalation**, name both tiers and why (e.g. ollama-fast → perplexity-coding).
- On **failure**, add **Failed:** `server` — reason — **Fallback:** `server`.

## Quick routing

| Intent | MCP |
|--------|-----|
| Official library/framework docs | context7 → @Docs → perplexity-search |
| Simple coding (single file, small scope) | ollama-fast |
| Complex coding (multi-file, hard bugs, new deps) | perplexity-coding |
| General web research (not lib docs) | perplexity-search |
| Codebase-only edits | No MCP — use repo tools |

## Documentation & research

For **API reference, hooks, config, versions** of a known library:

1. **context7** — `resolve-library-id` then `query-docs`
2. **Cursor @Docs** — if indexed or @Docs matches
3. **perplexity-search** — only when context7/@Docs cannot answer, or general web research

Do **not** use perplexity-search for lib API questions if context7 or @Docs can answer.

**perplexity-search** (`@plx-search`): comparisons, opinions, news, fallback after docs fail.

## ollama-fast (default for simple coding)

Use first for **low-complexity** work. User does **not** need to say “local”.

**Prefer when:** single file, ~&lt; 50 lines, one function/util/test, straightforward TS/JS, clear scope.

**Tools:** `list_models`, `show_model`, `ask_model` — default `qwen2.5-coder:14b` @ `http://localhost:11434`

**Requires:** `ollama serve` + model pulled. On failure → report **Failed: ollama-fast** and offer perplexity-coding.

## perplexity-coding (`@plx-code`)

**Prefer when:** multi-file, new deps/infra, hard bugs, security/performance/architecture, weak ollama output (after one retry).

**Tool:** `perplexity_search_web` · **Model:** `sonar-reasoning-pro` · preset `pro-search`  
**Requires:** `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY`

## perplexity-search (`@plx-search`)

Research **only** — not primary for large codegen unless asked.

**Tool:** `perplexity_search_web` · **Model:** `sonar` · web search only  
**Requires:** `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY`

## Manual overrides

Override defaults: `@plx-code`, `@plx-search`, `@ollama-fast`, explicit “use context7”.

## Complexity checklist

**2+ heavy signals → perplexity-coding** (skip ollama-first): 2+ files, new packages, context7 failed + needs web, auth/security/prod, large “architecture” asks.

## On failure

Report **Failed:** server + fix (API key, `ollama serve`, context7 library ID). Escalate one tier with user consent or if blocked.
